From: old-mac-halflife (Half-Life PPC port)
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: don't over-release CGDisplayAvailableModes on pre-10.6

Root cause of the SIGBUS-at-0x1 crash on Mac OS X 10.5 Leopard (PPC).

Cocoa_GetDisplayModes() picks its display-mode source by OS version:

  * >= 10.6 : CGDisplayCopyAllDisplayModes()  -- "Copy" rule, we OWN the array
  * <  10.6 : CGDisplayAvailableModes()        -- "Get"  rule, CoreGraphics owns it

...but it then called CFRelease(modes) unconditionally. On the <10.6 path that
is an over-release of an array CoreGraphics keeps in its own internal cache.
The array (and the mode dictionaries it holds) is freed underneath CG, so the
next CGDisplayCurrentMode() -- which HIToolbox's _FirstEventTime() calls to
timestamp the very first pumped event -- returns a dangling mode dictionary.
Reading it does objc_msgSend on freed memory => EXC_BAD_ACCESS / SIGBUS at 0x1,
deep inside Apple frameworks, on the first SDL_PollEvent/SDL_WaitEvent after the
app enumerates display modes (which Xash3D does at video init to build its
resolution list).

Minimal repro on the G5: SDL_Init(VIDEO) + SDL_GetNumDisplayModes() + one
SDL_PollEvent() crashes; without the mode enumeration it runs fine.

Fix: only CFRelease(modes) on the 10.6+ (Copy-rule) path, matching how the
per-mode CGDisplayModeRetain() a few lines up is already guarded.

--- a/src/video/cocoa/SDL_cocoamodes.m
+++ b/src/video/cocoa/SDL_cocoamodes.m
@@ -493,7 +493,17 @@ Cocoa_GetDisplayModes(_THIS, SDL_VideoDisplay * display)
         }

         CVDisplayLinkRelease(link);
-        CFRelease(modes);
+#if MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED >= 1060
+        /* CGDisplayCopyAllDisplayModes (>=10.6) follows the Copy rule, so we own
+         * this array and must release it. But on the <10.6 path above we used
+         * CGDisplayAvailableModes(), which follows the Get rule: the array is
+         * owned by CoreGraphics and shared with its internal cache. Releasing it
+         * there is an over-release that later makes CGDisplayCurrentMode() (called
+         * by HIToolbox _FirstEventTime on the first event pump) return a dangling
+         * mode dict -> objc_msgSend on freed memory -> SIGBUS at 0x1. So only
+         * release on 10.6+. (oldmac Leopard-PPC fix.) */
+        CFRelease(modes);
+#endif
     }
 }

